        "original_id": "2a6bd581-fb6b-539b-bb4f-340f9fcd8069",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Modern Records, Flair Records\n- People: Little Richard, Etta James, Joe Houston, Ike and Tina Turner, John Lee Hooker, the Bihari brothers\n- Events: Toronto Rock and Roll Revival festival\n- Works: Keep on Rockin'\n\nFacts:\n- Modern Music was an American record company and label formed in 1945 in Los Angeles by the Bihari brothers.\n- Little Richard, born Richard Wayne Penniman on December 5, 1932, is an American musician, singer, actor, comedian, and songwriter.\n- Modern Records was one of the major R&B labels in the 1950s and 1960s, with artists including Etta James, Joe Houston, Little Richard, Ike and Tina Turner, and John Lee Hooker.\n- Flair Records was a subsidiary of Modern Records.\n- Keep on Rockin' is a film of a 1969 Little Richard concert at the Toronto Rock and Roll Revival festival, and it was originally released in 1970.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5c908d7e-7dfd-5e2d-ac27-4ff600d52d19",
        "text": "Page: Modern Records. Sentence: Modern Music was an American record company and label formed in 1945 in Los Angeles by the Bihari brothers.\nPage: Modern Records. Sentence: Modern was also one of the big R&B labels with artists including Etta James, Joe Houston, Little Richard, Ike and Tina Turner and John Lee Hooker in the 1950s and 1960s.\nPage: Little Richard. Sentence: Richard Wayne Penniman (born December 5, 1932), known as Little Richard, is an American musician, singer, actor, comedian and songwriter.\nPage: Flair Records. Sentence: It was a subsidiary of Modern Records.\nPage: Keep On Rockin' (film). Sentence: Keep on Rockin', aka \"Little Richard: Keep on Rockin\" (United States video title) is a film of a 1969 Little Richard concert at the Toronto Rock and Roll Revival festival originally released in 1970.",
